is it even possible to wake up at 5am  feeling glorious  heck yes it is it is currently 5 45 as  i'm filming this and i'm super excited  to share this video with you today  because i'm going to share with you some  of the things that i do to be able to  help me to wake up between 4 30 and 5  a.m on a regular basis so if you've ever  tried to wake up at 5am and have failed  or have just tried to wake up earlier in  general consider this your call to give  it another try but this time with a few  changes that will ensure that you will  wake up every day without feeling a hot  miserable mess but before we begin if  you like this video please give it a  thumbs up and subscribe so that you  won't miss when i post a new video and  if you don't like it by all means thumbs  it down but please give me some feedback  in the comments so that i know what to  work on all right let's get started  before we can even address your morning  routine we first have to talk about your  nighttime routine because the key to  having a productive 5am routine  productive is to have an even better  nighttime routine the night before  because waking up early is not about  sleep deprivation empowering through  that actually the research is totally  clear that sleep deprivation can have  profound negative effects on your health  and your lifespan but besides that how  productive are you really being if your  brain is total mush because you didn't  sleep the night before so having an  awesome nighttime routine is imperative  this will ensure that you wake up  feeling well rested and ready to  dominate the day what does this amazing  nighttime routine look like you might  ask i got you covered  use science to your advantage like many  awesome built-in features your body has  it's your circadian rhythm that's  responsible for your sleep wake cycles  but through the exposure to blue light  through lighting in your home tv screens  computers and phones a hormone called  melatonin is suppressed and that's  really a bummer because that hormone is  responsible for making you sleepy so  what you're going to do is be like a  chicken we have chickens that roam  around free during the day but around  sundown they wander back into their coop  all on their own so what you're going to  do is take our chicken's advice around  sunset start turning off your devices  and have your phones set to  automatically change to night mode so  that they can cut down on blue light  start closing your curtains and if you  don't have blackout curtains i highly  recommend them this was something that i  tried when i worked night shift and it  really helped me out because i lived in  an area that was just highly lit so if  you live in a city maybe then perhaps  try blackout curtains and also just take  this time to tidy your home so that you  don't wake up feeling stressed and  anxious first thing in the morning when  you wake up because we have kids and our  nighttime routine involves getting them  ready for bed we usually start around  7pm so that most days we are in bed by  nine so find a time that works for you  but especially in the beginning give  yourself more time than you think you  need and if your phone is your alarm  have an automatic do not disturb so that  you do not get woken up with texts or  phone calls during the night and put  your phone to bed and i don't mean in  your bed have it across the room or  maybe even in another room to force you  to get out of the bed when it rings  use technology to your advantage so i  mentioned that our nighttime routine  begins around 7 pm and we actually have  smart bulbs that are scheduled to dim to  a warm light at 7 00 pm and this not  only means that our home automatically  becomes darker but it also sends a cue  ah it's bedtime and then in the morning  time they're set to 100 bright daylight  and especially on days when i really  don't want to get up it sends a message  to my eyeballs see that yessie see it it  is time to get up another thing that we  do is we set the thermostat to a lower  temperature at night and this actually  lowers your core temperature it kind of  tells your body to wind down our  daughter has hypersensitivity especially  to sounds and so she has a sound machine  that helps her sleep really well at  night but for me my go-to is ear plugs  because if my husband snores not only  does that mean that i can sleep but he  can sleep as well because i'm not like  elbowing him the entire night the ones  that i have are silicone and washable  and they really are help to me and this  was also one of those things that i kind  of picked up once i worked night shift  because if you've ever worked night  shift you know that you have to have  like impeccable habits to be able to get  the sleep that you need and you  definitely don't have to get any of  these things but if you have them use  them to your advantage because it will  help kind of create an ambience that  will promote sleep  recently i witnessed and assisted in a  traumatic head-on collision between a  dump truck and another vehicle and i  have worked in icu for years i've been  in emergency situations but i had never  been in the scene of an accident before  and it left me shocked for several days  i really struggled to fall asleep  without seeing or hearing those images  in my brain and to sleep without  dreaming about it all night long and so  i have been very diligent to practice  gratitude every night before bed and it  may sound so silly it may sound like a  pointless waste of time but i assure you  for me it feels like it's almost like  i'm priming my brain priming my  subconscious to think of positive  thoughts and to perceive positive  thoughts while i'm sleeping and i find  that not only do i dream much more happy  dreams i sleep much better and i wake up  feeling so much better the next day so  tonight when you're in bed and you have  your eyes closed make those last  thoughts that you think of a positive  thing it could be something like you're  being hopeful for the next day and  you're picturing in your mind how  awesome it's going to be but just  practice gratitude you'd be surprised  how awesome and what a calming effect it  can have on you don't knock it till you  try it all right enough about nighttime  routines how do you actually wake up at  5am feeling glorious  have you ever been so excited about  something that you couldn't sleep the  night before or you kept waking up  through the night because you thought it  was time to get up that's because when  you have a reason for why you're waking  up early or a motivation your brain  wakes up with a rush of happy hormones  that give you that boost of energy that  you need to get your butt out of bed you  have to romanticize the idea of waking  up early basically trick your brain into  seeing it as a pleasing thing to do or a  habit that you enjoy so ask yourself why  you're doing it to begin with what's  your purpose what do you plan on doing  have a clear picture in your mind for  the next day i can't tell you the number  of times i woke up early without having  a plan for the next day and you know  what i ended up doing when that happened  yeah going back to bed because i had  nothing to do  fail don't do this have a plan in place  for the next day another tip that i have  for you is to include something in that  plan that is specifically for your  enjoyment this is what james clear calls  habit stacking and basically what that  is is taking a habit that you already do  enjoy and pairing that with the habit  that you're trying to adopt that is not  enjoyable so for example if you're  waking up early to do taxes and you are  totally not excited about that then pair  that with something that you do enjoy  and this could be something as simple as  having an extra 10 minutes to get your  winged liner looking pristine having a  breakfast that you enjoy for me it's  lattes matcha latte chai latte cafe  latte i love me all things latte there's  just something cozy about a latte in the  morning that just brings me joy and it  brings a bit of yay to my morning so  find what those things are for you and  add them to your morning routine this  will help you actually enjoy waking up  early because it's more about you and  what you get to do  [Music]  and finally the day of here's some  things to consider first let's talk  about your alarm because the alarm that  you use can have a huge impact on how  you start your day that obnoxious loud  buzzing alarm never fails to wake me  with anxiety my heart rate shoots up and  instantly i start my day with stress  yeah that is not the right ringtone for  me you can try nature sounds a slow rise  that just slowly gets louder as time  progresses or if you're guilty of  pressing the snooze one too many times  then the math app can be your savior  basically what this does is that it  forces you to do puzzles before you can  turn off the alarm and this kind of  wakes up your brain whether you want it  to or not but whatever alarm that you  choose make sure that a it wakes you up  and b  it doesn't scare the heck out of you if  for whatever reason you still decided to  keep your alarm next to you maybe you  don't want to wake someone else up i  highly recommend mel robbins technique  and that is to count backwards from five  four three two one and just like a  rocket blast out of bed and what this  does is it basically forces you to act  before your brain can even react because  let's face it your brain will just tell  you to sleep in those first few seconds  are where you meet the most resistance  so as soon as your feet are on the  ground just know the hard part is over  with and you did it so now go hydrate  yourself splash some cold water on your  face go make yourself a latte and  conquer your day that is it for today's  video i thank you so much for watching  and if you liked this video and found it  helpful please give it a thumbs up and  subscribe so you won't miss when i post  a new video and let me know what are you  going to do with your morning routines i  can't wait to hear from you in the  comments and see you in the next video  bye for now  [Music]

